---
import CommercialLayout from '../layouts/CommercialLayout.astro';
---

<CommercialLayout
  title="Services"
  description="Route a broken handoff, new workflow, ongoing verification, website project, or larger custom software need to the right Toledo service."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="commercial-shell page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <h1 class="commercial-title">
          Start with the problem the business can observe.
        </h1><p>
          The smallest responsible scope comes first. Workflow units cover one
          supported handoff. Existing fixed products, websites, custom software,
          and discovery remain available when the problem is wider.
        </p>
      </div><div
        class="sleeve-mark"
        aria-label="Toledo Technologies service catalog sleeve"
      >
        <div class="sleeve-mark__label">
          <span>TT—SERVICES</span><span>Written delivery</span>
        </div><strong>Route by failure, not by fashion.</strong><p>
          One problem. A named result. Evidence before adjectives.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="offer-ledger">
        <article class="offer-row">
          <div>
            <h2>A handoff is broken</h2><p class="offer-price">$1,500</p>
          </div><p>One reproducible failure in one supported workflow.</p><div>
            <p>
              Choose Workflow Repair when the expected and actual result can be
              shown.
            </p><a href="/workflows/">Read Repair scope</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="offer-row">
          <div>
            <h2>A workflow is missing</h2><p class="offer-price">$3,000</p>
          </div><p>One deterministic event-to-result path.</p><div>
            <p>
              Choose Workflow Setup when the trigger, destination, and
              acceptance result are known.
            </p><a href="/workflows/">Read Setup scope</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="offer-row">
          <div>
            <h2>An accepted path needs checks</h2><p class="offer-price">
              $500/month
            </p>
          </div><p>One registered workflow with safe, authorized checks.</p><div
          >
            <p>
              Workflow Care is narrow. Broader application and website Care
              plans remain separate.
            </p><a href="/workflows/care/">Read the Care register</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="offer-row">
          <div>
            <h2>The cause is unknown</h2><p class="offer-price">$1,200</p>
          </div><p>
            Integration Triage diagnoses the boundary and recommends the next
            action.
          </p><div>
            <p>
              This existing engagement does not promise a repair and has no
              automatic Repair credit.
            </p><a href="/engagements/">See bounded engagements</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="offer-row">
          <div>
            <h2>A business needs its own tool</h2><p class="offer-price">
              From $5,500
            </p>
          </div><p>
            Bounded internal tools, dashboards, reviewed document processing,
            quote preparation, or staff knowledge assistants.
          </p><div>
            <p>
              Custom work uses the same one-project slot and is quoted
              separately from Setup and Care.
            </p><a href="/custom-tools/">Check custom-tool fit</a>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="offer-row">
          <div>
            <h2>The website itself needs work</h2><p class="offer-price">
              Separate practice
            </p>
          </div><p>
            Editorial websites, measured migrations, retain-or-repair decisions,
            performance work, and broader care.
          </p><div>
            <p>
              The six Toledo practices keep their own visual and commercial
              identity.
            </p><a href="https://web.toledotechnologies.com">Visit Toledo Web</a
            > · <a href="https://sitelift.toledotechnologies.com"
              >Visit SiteLift</a
            >
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Existing fixed products stay intact.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          File conversion remains $850 with its existing scope and refund
          condition. The evaluation harness remains $2,200 with its existing
          acceptance rule. The $1,200 Integration Triage remains diagnosis
          rather than a promised fix. Nothing on this page changes those
          purchase terms.
        </p>
      </div><div class="commercial-actions">
        <a class="commercial-action" href="/engagements/"
          >Review existing engagements</a
        ><a class="commercial-action commercial-action--text" href="/discovery/"
          >Review discovery products</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="commercial-section">
    <div class="commercial-shell">
      <div class="commercial-section__head">
        <h2>Specialist practices and owned products.</h2><p
          class="commercial-section__intro"
        >
          A workflow brief is the front door, not a reason to erase the work
          already available elsewhere in the Toledo catalog.
        </p>
      </div><div class="boundary-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Editorial websites and migrations</h3><p>
            Toledo Web projects retain the existing $5,500–$250,000+ range.
            SiteLift WordPress-exit migrations retain the existing
            $3,500–$65,000+ range, including retain-or-repair as a valid
            outcome.
          </p><a href="https://web.toledotechnologies.com">Visit Toledo Web</a>
          · <a href="https://sitelift.toledotechnologies.com">Visit SiteLift</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Custom applications</h3><p>
            Toledo Apps retains the existing $15,000–$750,000+ range for larger
            internal tools, portals, and custom software. A smaller workflow or
            bounded tool is considered first when it can solve the problem.
          </p><a href="https://apps.toledotechnologies.com">Visit Toledo Apps</a
          >
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>AI workflow and agent design</h3><p>
            Task-level automation with explicit rules, model-assisted steps,
            permissions, and recorded outcomes. The broader AI practice retains
            its existing $10,000–$300,000+ range.
          </p><a href="https://ai.toledotechnologies.com/#start"
            >AI Automation Blueprint ($3,500–$10,000)</a
          >
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Native mobile</h3><p>
            Discovery for work that genuinely requires device permissions,
            offline behavior, or native platform constraints. Existing project
            floors remain $50,000+ native and $65,000+ cross-platform.
          </p><a href="https://mobile.toledotechnologies.com/#discovery"
            >Delphi Mobile Discovery ($5,000–$7,500)</a
          >
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Tessera compliance evidence</h3><p>
            Toledo-operated software, separate from custom engagements: <span
              >PCI DSS 6.4.3 remediation pack ($299 once)</span
            >, a <span>PCI DSS 5.4.1 email-authentication pack ($99 once)</span
            >, and a one-target PCI DSS 11.6.1 evidence ledger ($99/month). It
            reports evidence and limits; it does not determine PCI DSS
            compliance.
          </p><a
            href="https://qi.toledotechnologies.com/pci-4-compliance-scanner"
            >Inspect Tessera evidence</a
          >
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Free served-HTML inventory</h3><p>
            The Free MIT served-HTML inventory Action lists scripts in returned
            HTML. It does not execute JavaScript and does not certify
            compliance.
          </p><a href="https://github.com/ntoledo319/pci-payment-page-check"
            >Read the source</a
          > · <a
            href="https://github.com/marketplace/actions/pci-payment-page-script-check"
            >GitHub Marketplace Action</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="commercial-section__intro">
        Half of the discovery fee credits toward the kickoff Project Retainer if
        you proceed within 30 days. The credit is capped at that Project
        Retainer; unused credit lapses and does not roll forward.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CommercialLayout>
